-- FRM-706 lists the sample points for the collector; FSQM-015 names the rounds and one test per point.
-- Both are still DRAFT (D-16).
--
-- Owner, 2026-10-07: the results log should already show where to swab and what each swab is tested
-- for. Two decisions that also had to go into the program so the two cannot disagree:
--   * ONE TEST PER POINT. Zone 1 and Zone 2 points: Enterobacteriaceae. Zone 3 and Zone 4 points:
--     Listeria species. Only the two points swabbed every round (dunk sink inside, perforated tray)
--     get both.
--   * FIXED ROUNDS. Three rounds a year, each with its own points (6, 5 and 5) plus the two swabbed
--     every round. 10, 9 and 9 tests.
--
-- FRM-706: the sample grid becomes a fixed list of 20 lines (18 points, two of them twice), each with
-- its round, when it is swabbed and what it is tested for already entered. RESULTS ARE NEVER PREFILLED.
-- A line not swabbed in a round is marked "Not sampled this round" or deleted. A "Round" field is added.
-- FRM-706 has no entries (guarded). One UPDATE per document.

begin;

do $guard$
declare d record;
begin
  select status, md5(content::text) as cmd5 into d from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FSQM-015';
  if d.status is distinct from 'draft' or d.cmd5 <> '2e7fc40547b2282108d7152b0617289c' then
    raise exception 'FSQM-015 is not the draft this migration expects (%).', d.cmd5;
  end if;
  select status, md5(content::text) as cmd5 into d from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FRM-706';
  if d.status is distinct from 'draft' or d.cmd5 <> 'd101612f2d62a048a9b43838d1a90fc9' then
    raise exception 'FRM-706 is not the draft this migration expects (%).', d.cmd5;
  end if;
  if exists (select 1 from public.sop_document_responses r join public.sop_documents x on x.id = r.document_id
              where x.sop_number = 'FRM-706') then
    raise exception 'FRM-706 already has entries; its sample grid cannot be reshaped.';
  end if;
end $guard$;

update public.sop_documents
   set content = jsonb_set(content, '{procedure}', $q$["Why this program exists", "• The oven is the only step that kills bacteria. After it the product cools in its molds on covered racks, is depanned onto a table, is dunked and drained on a perforated tray, and is placed on a baking tray before it goes into its pouch. All of that time it is open to the room.", "• Anything living in the room can reach the product then, and nothing later kills it. This program looks for it in the room, because testing finished product rarely finds a problem that sits in one corner of a room (SQF 2.4.8.1).", "What it covers", "• The production room on all three days of the rotation, the packaging materials storage, the warehouse where finished product is held, and the break area.", "• Not covered: testing of ingredients, packaging or product. The site inspects product and does not analyse it (FSQM-014). Every sample here is taken from the room.", "• Not covered: ambient air testing and the other high-risk process clauses (SQF 11.7.1.1 to 11.7.1.5). FSQM-013 records that the site processes no high-risk food, so those clauses are not engaged. HIGH CARE on FSQM-039 is the site's own name for where product is open after the oven; it is not a high-risk area under the Code. This is looked at again when the water activity of the finished product is measured.", "Zones and sample points", "• Every sample point is in one of four zones, by how close it is to open product. The zones are not the hygiene areas drawn on FSQM-039: an area says what may happen in a place, a zone says what a result found there would mean.", "• Zone 1 - surfaces that touch open product.", "◦ 1-A Depanning table top", "◦ 1-B Dunk sink, inside", "◦ 1-C Perforated dunking tray", "◦ 1-D Baking tray the dunked product is placed on", "• Zone 2 - surfaces close to Zone 1 that do not touch product. The vacuum sealer is here because the product is already in its pouch when it reaches it.", "◦ 2-A Cooling rack shelf, where the pans sit", "◦ 2-B Cooling rack cover, inside", "◦ 2-C Cooling rack upright and castor", "◦ 2-D Dunk sink, outside and stand", "◦ 2-E Vacuum sealer, bed, seal bar, lid and control panel", "◦ 2-F Kettle, outside and tilt handle", "• Zone 3 - the rest of the production room.", "◦ 3-A Floor under the cooling racks", "◦ 3-B Floor at the dunk sink (in use)", "◦ 3-C Floor drain nearest the dunk sink (in use)", "◦ 3-D Hand-wash sink, taps and basin", "◦ 3-E Mop sink and cleaning tools", "◦ 3-F Waste bin, lid and rim (in use)", "• Zone 4 - outside the production room.", "◦ 4-A Warehouse floor at the door from production", "◦ 4-B Break area table", "• Each point keeps its number, so its results can be compared over time. A point is added, moved or removed by revising this list, never on the day.", "• The dunk area matters most. It holds raw batter on Day 1 and baked product on Day 2, and only the changeover clean separates the two.", "What is tested for", "• Enterobacteriaceae, on every Zone 1 and Zone 2 point, as a check that the cleaning is working.", "• Listeria species, on every Zone 3 and Zone 4 point, and on the two Zone 1 points swabbed every round: the inside of the dunk sink and the perforated dunking tray. The dunk is a wet step after the oven, and floors, drains and sinks are where Listeria settles. The whole genus is tested for, not only Listeria monocytogenes, because it shows a problem sooner.", "• Salmonella is not tested for on the raw side, because everything there goes through the bake. This is looked at again if raw-side material could ever reach product after the oven: rework, a topping added cold, or a shared utensil.", "• These choices are looked at again when the water activity of the finished, sealed product is measured (FSQM-016). If the product cannot support growth, testing leans to Enterobacteriaceae, with Listeria less often (SQF 2.4.8.2 i).", "When and how samples are taken", "• A round of swabs is taken at least every four months (SQF 2.4.8.2 ii).", "• A year has three rounds. Each is the two points swabbed every round - the inside of the dunk sink and the perforated dunking tray - and that round's own points, so that every point is sampled at least once a year (SQF 2.4.8.2 iii).", "◦ Round 1: 1-A, 2-A, 2-D, 3-B, 3-C, 4-A", "◦ Round 2: 1-D, 2-B, 2-E, 3-A, 3-D", "◦ Round 3: 2-C, 2-F, 3-E, 3-F, 4-B", "• FRM-706 lists every point with its round and what it is tested for. The lines for the round are swabbed; the others are marked not sampled.", "• The round is taken on a Day 2 morning, after the changeover clean and before dunking starts. A bad result then points at the clean, which can be put right, and not at a batch already made. Points marked (in use) are swabbed during or just after the run.", "• No point is cleaned specially because it is about to be swabbed.", "• Swabs are taken by the SQF Practitioner, or by a person the SQF Practitioner has trained (FRM-952), in the way the laboratory instructs, and are sent the day they are taken.", "• An extra round is taken after an unsatisfactory result (Part 7) and after a change to the floor, the process or the clean.", "The laboratory", "• Samples are analysed by an outside laboratory accredited to ISO/IEC 17025, or an equivalent standard, for the tests it does for the site.", "• The laboratory is entered on FRM-206, with its accreditation, before the first sample is sent.", "• The test method, its detection limit and the reporting time are those on the laboratory's report, which is attached to FRM-706.", "• FSQM-014 says no outside laboratory is used. That is about product and stays true. FSQM-014 is amended to say so when this program is issued.", "An unsatisfactory result", "• A presumptive positive is acted on as a positive. Confirmation is asked for, and the work starts without waiting for it (SQF 2.4.8.2 iv).", "• More swabs are taken around the point - what it drains to, sits on, touches or shares a route with - to find where the organism is living.", "• The point is cleaned and sanitized, then swabbed again until three results in a row are clear.", "• If the organism comes back at the same point, the cause is put right - standing water, a cracked surface, a hollow frame, a clean that cannot reach - and not only the surface.", "• Where the result is on a Zone 1 surface, the product that touched it is held on FRM-702 (FSQM-018) and is not released (FSQM-020) until the SQF Practitioner decides what is done with it.", "• A CAPA is raised on FRM-007 where FSQM-009 requires one, and always for a confirmed Listeria result in Zone 1.", "Records and review", "• Every round is recorded on FRM-706 Environmental Monitoring Results Log: each sample with its point, organism and result, with the laboratory's report attached.", "• The SQF Practitioner reads the results when they arrive and reports them in the next monthly update on FRM-009. The year's results are reviewed at the management review on FRM-001 (SQF 2.4.8.3).", "• A trend is: the same point positive more than once, counts rising at any point, positives that share a drain or a route, or a listed point that was not sampled. A trend is acted on through FSQM-009.", "• This program is reviewed every year, and sooner when the floor, the process or the clean changes, when the water activity is measured, or when the results show the points are in the wrong places."]$q$::jsonb)
 where sop_number = 'FSQM-015' and status = 'draft';

update public.sop_documents
   set content = jsonb_set(content, '{form_schema}', $q${"schemaVersion": 1, "settings": {"attachmentsEnabled": true, "allowMultipleDrafts": true, "requireVerification": true, "instanceTitleTemplate": "{round} - {date}"}, "sections": [{"id": "round", "title": "1. The sampling round", "fields": [{"id": "how_this_works", "type": "info", "label": "How to use this", "text": "One record for each sampling round (FSQM-015). Section 2 lists every sample point with its round and what it is tested for. Swab the lines marked \"Every round\" and the lines for this round. Mark every other line \"Not sampled this round\", or delete it. Save a draft on the day. When the laboratory report comes back, enter each result, attach the report, complete section 3 and submit. Do not clean a sample point specially because it is about to be swabbed."}, {"id": "round", "type": "select", "label": "Round", "width": "third", "required": true, "showInList": true, "options": ["Round 1", "Round 2", "Round 3", "Extra round"]}, {"id": "reason", "type": "select", "label": "Reason", "width": "third", "required": true, "showInList": true, "options": ["Routine round", "Re-test after an unsatisfactory result", "Vector swabs around an unsatisfactory result", "After a change to the floor, the process or the clean"]}, {"id": "date", "type": "date", "label": "Date sampled", "width": "third", "required": true, "showInList": true}, {"id": "rotation_day", "type": "select", "label": "Day of the rotation", "width": "third", "required": true, "options": ["Day 1 - bake", "Day 2 - dip and seal", "Day 3 - package", "No production"]}, {"id": "laboratory", "type": "text", "label": "Laboratory", "width": "third", "required": true, "help": "As listed on FRM-206"}, {"id": "date_sent", "type": "date", "label": "Date sent", "width": "third", "required": true}, {"id": "report_ref", "type": "text", "label": "Laboratory report no.", "width": "third", "required": true}, {"id": "date_reported", "type": "date", "label": "Date reported", "width": "third", "required": true}]}, {"id": "samples", "title": "2. Samples", "fields": [{"id": "samples", "type": "grid", "label": "Sample points", "required": true, "rowDialog": true, "help": "One line for each swab. A swab taken somewhere not listed is added with Add sample.", "columns": [{"id": "round", "label": "Round", "type": "select", "width": 1, "options": ["Every round", "Round 1", "Round 2", "Round 3", "Extra"]}, {"id": "state", "label": "When", "type": "select", "required": true, "width": 1.3, "options": ["After cleaning, before production", "In use"]}, {"id": "organism", "label": "Tested for", "type": "select", "required": true, "width": 1.2, "options": ["Listeria species", "Enterobacteriaceae", "Other - say which in Notes"]}, {"id": "time", "label": "Time", "type": "text", "width": 0.7}, {"id": "result", "label": "Result", "type": "select", "required": true, "width": 1.3, "options": ["Not detected", "Within the limit", "ABOVE THE LIMIT", "PRESUMPTIVE POSITIVE", "CONFIRMED POSITIVE", "Not sampled this round"]}, {"id": "count", "label": "Count, if reported", "type": "text", "width": 1}, {"id": "method", "label": "Method (as on the report)", "type": "text", "width": 1}, {"id": "notes", "label": "Notes", "type": "text", "width": 1.5}], "rows": {"mode": "fixed", "labels": ["1-B Dunk sink, inside", "1-B Dunk sink, inside", "1-C Perforated dunking tray", "1-C Perforated dunking tray", "1-A Depanning table top", "2-A Cooling rack shelf, where the pans sit", "2-D Dunk sink, outside and stand", "3-B Floor at the dunk sink (in use)", "3-C Floor drain nearest the dunk sink (in use)", "4-A Warehouse floor at the door from production", "1-D Baking tray the dunked product is placed on", "2-B Cooling rack cover, inside", "2-E Vacuum sealer, bed, seal bar, lid and control panel", "3-A Floor under the cooling racks", "3-D Hand-wash sink, taps and basin", "2-C Cooling rack upright and castor", "2-F Kettle, outside and tilt handle", "3-E Mop sink and cleaning tools", "3-F Waste bin, lid and rim (in use)", "4-B Break area table"], "defaultValues": [{"round": "Every round", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Every round", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Every round", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Every round", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 1", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 1", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 1", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 1", "state": "In use", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 1", "state": "In use", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 1", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 2", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 2", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 2", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 2", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 2", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 3", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 3", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Enterobacteriaceae"}, {"round": "Round 3", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 3", "state": "In use", "organism": "Listeria species"}, {"round": "Round 3", "state": "After cleaning, before production", "organism": "Listeria species"}], "deletable": true, "labelHeader": "Sample point", "addLabel": "Add sample"}}]}, {"id": "outcome", "title": "3. Result and actions", "fields": [{"id": "overall", "type": "select", "label": "Overall", "width": "half", "required": true, "showInList": true, "options": ["All satisfactory", "One or more unsatisfactory"]}, {"id": "actions", "type": "textarea", "label": "If unsatisfactory: what was done", "help": "The vector swabs, the clean and re-swab, and what was found to be the cause (FSQM-015 Part 7)"}, {"id": "hold_ref", "type": "text", "label": "Hold record (FRM-702), if product was held", "width": "half"}, {"id": "capa_no", "type": "text", "label": "CAPA Report no. (FRM-007)", "width": "half"}]}, {"id": "sign", "title": "4. Sign-off", "fields": [{"id": "sampled_by", "type": "signature", "label": "Sampled by", "role": "filler", "required": true, "statement": "I took these samples at the points and times shown, and no point was cleaned specially beforehand."}, {"id": "reviewed_by", "type": "signature", "label": "Results reviewed by the SQF Practitioner", "role": "verifier", "required": true, "statement": "I have read the laboratory report. The results above are as reported and the actions are as stated."}]}]}$q$::jsonb)
 where sop_number = 'FRM-706' and status = 'draft';

do $verify$
declare d record; g jsonb; n int;
begin
  select status, revision, approved_by, content into d from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FSQM-015';
  if d.status <> 'draft' or d.revision <> 'New' or d.approved_by is not null then raise exception 'FSQM-015 status changed.'; end if;
  if jsonb_array_length(d.content->'procedure') <> 66 then raise exception 'FSQM-015 procedure length is wrong.'; end if;
  if md5((d.content - 'procedure')::text) <> '46fada3ac98cbdd32eb0d4904a021fbc' then raise exception 'a section of FSQM-015 other than the procedure changed.'; end if;

  select content->'form_schema'->'sections'->1->'fields'->0 into g from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FRM-706' and status = 'draft';
  if g->'rows'->>'mode' <> 'fixed' or jsonb_array_length(g->'rows'->'labels') <> 20
     or jsonb_array_length(g->'rows'->'defaultValues') <> 20 then
    raise exception 'FRM-706 sample grid is not the 20-line list.';
  end if;
  -- every point in the program is a line on the form, and every line is a point in the program
  select count(*) into n from jsonb_array_elements_text(d.content->'procedure') l
   where l ~ '^◦ [1-4]-[A-F] ' and (g->'rows'->'labels') ? substr(l, 3);
  if n <> 18 or exists (select 1 from jsonb_array_elements_text(g->'rows'->'labels') lb
                         where not (d.content->'procedure') ? ('◦ ' || lb)) then
    raise exception 'the sample points in FSQM-015 and on FRM-706 do not match.';
  end if;
  -- no result, count or time is prefilled
  if exists (select 1 from jsonb_array_elements(g->'rows'->'defaultValues') v
              where v ? 'result' or v ? 'count' or v ? 'time' or v ? 'method' or not (v ? 'round' and v ? 'state' and v ? 'organism')) then
    raise exception 'FRM-706 prefills something it must not, or misses a planned value.';
  end if;
  -- one test per point: Zone 1 and 2 Enterobacteriaceae, Zone 3 and 4 Listeria; only 1-B and 1-C carry both
  if exists (select 1 from jsonb_array_elements_text(g->'rows'->'labels') with ordinality a(lb, i)
               join jsonb_array_elements(g->'rows'->'defaultValues') with ordinality b(v, j) on i = j
              where left(lb, 3) not in ('1-B', '1-C')
                and (v->>'organism') <> case when left(lb, 1) in ('1', '2') then 'Enterobacteriaceae' else 'Listeria species' end) then
    raise exception 'a point is prefilled with the wrong test.';
  end if;
  if (select count(*) from public.sop_documents x, jsonb_array_elements(x.content->'form_schema'->'sections') s,
                           jsonb_array_elements(s->'fields') f where x.sop_number = 'FRM-706') <> 16 then
    raise exception 'FRM-706 field count is wrong.';
  end if;
  if exists (select 1 from public.sop_documents where sop_number in ('FSQM-015', 'FRM-706')
              and content::text ~* 'Production Supervisor|Diana|Gabriela|Christina|GJM|Mercer|Pillsbury|Amazon|Sysco|Bahamas') then
    raise exception 'a D-16 document names a person, a supplier or a customer.';
  end if;
end $verify$;

commit;
